<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard to cut Vecta prices.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard to cut Vecta prices.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co is set to cut prices nearly across the board on its Vectra commercial and high performance personal computer, on Thursday morning, according to a spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The Palo Alto-based computer maker is also expected to include Microsoft Corp's Windows NT 4.0 with its new models equipped with Intel Corp's Pentium Pro processors.</p>
<p>Details were not immediately available.</p>
</text>
